meta {
  name: Create Incident Record
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngPersonId/incidents
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 2
  youngPersonId: 4
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "incident_datetime": "2026-01-15 14:30:00",
    "reported_by": 2,
    "location_of_incident": "Common Room",
    "severity_of_incident": "moderate",
    "any_witnesses": "John Doe, Jane Smith observed the incident",
    "transport_used": "House vehicle - Ford Transit",
    "clothing_jewellery_worn": "Blue hoodie, jeans, white trainers, silver bracelet",
    "young_persons_involved": [84, 91],
    "agency_staff_involved": [10]
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Incident Record
  
  Creates a new incident/accident record. This is the first step - only basic incident details are required initially.
  
  ## Required Fields:
  - `incident_datetime` (string) - Date and time of incident (format: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS)
  - `reported_by` (integer) - User ID of person reporting (staff member)
  - `location_of_incident` (string) - Location where incident occurred
  - `severity_of_incident` (string) - Severity level: minor, moderate, major, critical
  
  ## Optional Fields:
  - `any_witnesses` (string) - Text description of witnesses
  - `transport_used` (string) - Transportation involved description
  - `clothing_jewellery_worn` (string) - Description of clothing/jewellery worn
  
  ## Staff/YP Involved (Multi-select):
  
  - `young_persons_involved` (array of integers) - Array of Young Person IDs involved
  - `staff_involved` (array of integers) - Array of Staff User IDs involved
  - `agency_staff_involved` (array of integers) - Array of Agency Staff (EmployeeJob) IDs
  
  **Example:**
  ```json
  {
    "young_persons_involved": [1, 2, 3],
    "staff_involved": [5, 6, 8],
    "agency_staff_involved": [10, 12]
  }
  ```
  
  ## Validation Rules:
  - `staff_involved.*` must exist in `users` table
  - `agency_staff_involved.*` must exist in `employee_jobs` table
  - `young_persons_involved.*` must exist in `young_persons` table
  
  ## Severity Options:
  - `minor` - Minor incident
  - `moderate` - Moderate incident
  - `major` - Major incident (triggers manager notification)
  - `critical` - Critical incident (triggers manager notification)
  
  ## Response:
  Returns the created incident with loaded relationships:
  - `staff_involved[]` - Staff members involved
  - `agency_staff_involved[]` - Agency staff involved
  - `young_persons_involved[]` - Young persons involved
  
  ## Note:
  The pivot tables have `role_in_incident` and `involvement_description` columns for future use,
  but currently only IDs are stored. Roles/descriptions can be added later when UI supports it.
  - Status & Sign-off
}
